\section{2. Zero-Python Architecture (Native C++ Runtime)}{
Unlike standard Python-dependent deep learning packages, \code{pliman} executes ONNX models
natively in C++ via direct Microsoft ONNX Runtime C API dynamic bindings.
\itemize{
\item \strong{Zero Python Requirement:} No Python, Conda, Virtualenv, or pip required.
\item \strong{Direct C++ Binding:} Connects directly to Microsoft's official ONNX Runtime C++ engine (\code{onnxruntime.dll} on Windows / \code{libonnxruntime.so} on Linux / \code{libonnxruntime.dylib} on macOS).
\item \strong{CPU & GPU Support:} Runs optimized CPU multi-threading (AVX2/AVX512) or CUDA GPU acceleration.
}
}

\section{3. Model Weight Storage & Cache}{
Downloaded \code{.onnx} model weights are stored permanently in the user's R data directory:
\code{tools::R_user_dir("pliman", which = "data")/models}
(e.g., \verb{C:/Users/<User>/AppData/Local/R/data/R/pliman/models} on Windows).
This follows CRAN policy and ensures models are preserved across R session restarts
and package upgrades.
}

